### Expected behaviour

The UPF should validate URR-ID from PFCP messages before using it as an index into sess->urr_acc. If urr->id is zero or greater than OGS_MAX_NUM_OF_URR, the Session Establishment Request should be rejected gracefully (e.g. with an error response), and the process should not abort.

### Observed Behaviour

A single crafted PFCP Session Establishment Request with CreateURR(URR-ID = 65535) and ISTM=1 causes upf_sess_urr_acc_timers_setup() to fail its internal assertion and abort the open5gs-upfd process, leading to a denial of service.

