### Expected behaviour

The UPF should validate the Outer Header Creation IE by its length is non-zero and consistent with its encoded subfields.
If a malformed encoding is detected, the UPF should treat it as invalid input and handle the error gracefully.

### Observed Behaviour

When the UPF receives a PFCP Session Establishment Request containing a CreateFAR whose Forwarding Parameters include an Outer Header Creation IE with an invalid (zero) length, the UPF crashes.

### eNodeB/gNodeB

No

### UE Models and versions

No

### Open5GS Release, Revision, or Tag

v2.7.6



### Description
Open5GS UPF v2.7.6 accepts a PFCP Session Establishment Request that installs a forwarding rule (FAR) whose Forwarding Parameters → Destination Interface is set to 2 (SGi-LAN / N6-LAN). However, the UPF GTP-U receive path (src/upf/gtp-path.c, _gtpv1_u_recv_cb) does not implement handling for DestinationInterface=2.
As a result, once any subsequent GTP-U packet matches the installed PDR and triggers the FAR forwarding path, the UPF reaches an unimplemented branch and terminates the process via a fatal assertion/abort, causing a user-plane denial of service (DoS).

