### Description

Open5GS UPF crashes with a NULL pointer dereference in ogs_ipfw_compile_rule() when processing a PFCP Session Establishment Request whose CreatePDR → PDI → SDF Filter contains an invalid or incomplete Flow-Description string (e.g., an empty string or one missing direction like "permit"). In these cases, the SDF Filter carries the FD flag, but the Flow-Description data is invalid, which causes ogs_ipfw_compile_rule() to dereference a NULL pointer, causing UPF to crash and leading to DoS.


